// GPU class: low-tablet
//
// States the smallest shipped class of device: a texture edge of 256 voxels and
// 1 GB of texture memory. Almost every volume exceeds that edge, so a viewport
// reduces its texture, and the reduction is easy to see.
//
// Use this profile to show what a reduction looks like. Compare it with
// `gpu/high`, which reduces far less, and with `gpu/high-texture-4096`, which
// reduces nothing.
//
// The profile is a stated value and not a measurement. Nothing probes the
// device, so a real device may hold more than this profile states.
//
// Load it with `?customization=gpu/low-tablet`.
{
  "bootstrap": {
    "cornerstone.gpuCapabilityProfile": "low-tablet"
  }
}
